Seriously, soldier ants are the number one killer on NAO. You did
several things wrong here:

1. If you're strong enough to last *five turns* surrounded by ants,
you had plenty of time to engrave dust Elbereth.
2. If you saw the first ant coming, you had time to flee to a corridor
and pick those ants off one by one. This *was* the main dungeon, after
all.
If you're in the mines, well, it's not as clear-cut. I'd have tried
escaping.
3. You were destroying a dwarf zombie near ants. Cardinal sin. One
dwarf zombie nearby is one less ant.
4. You were past dlvl:9 and didn't use one of Sokoban's guaranteed
scrolls of earth. Even then, it's worth reading an unidentified
noncursed 200 zorkmid scroll in this situation if you've got nothing
else, because taming
and earth will save you and amnesia won't do much *immediately* bad.
Long term: amnesia SUCKS. Short term, not so much.

Point 2 bears repeating. Never, *ever* get surrounded. And if you're
surrounded anyway, don't fight. STOP. It doesn't matter what kind of
enemy it is, STOP and think. You will most likely have a solution in
inventory in the form of escape item, conflict, scroll of earth, wand
of death, wand of sleep, or other strong wand. Consider them in that
order, more or less. In some situations (e.g. cockatrice is close by),
you may want conflict first.
